        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "baebd1e7-f50d-573d-a3f3-c3dbb91cc6c9",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Eardwulf, Æthelred I, Ælfwald II, Æthelwald Moll, Æthelthryth, Alhred\n- Places: Northumbria\n- Topics: Northumbrian kingship, dynastic strife, deposition, assassination, succession\n\nFacts:\n- In 774, Æthelred I became king of Northumbria, possibly while still a child, after Alhred was deposed.\n- Æthelred I was the son of Æthelwald Moll and Æthelthryth.\n- Æthelred I ruled Northumbria from 774 to 779.\n- In 790, Æthelred I began a second reign as king of Northumbria.\n- In 790, during dynastic strife among several noble families in Northumbria, Æthelred I attempted to have Eardwulf assassinated.\n- On 18 April 796, Æthelred I was murdered, ending his second reign.\n- Eardwulf may have had a second reign in Northumbria beginning in 808 and lasting until perhaps 811 or 830.\n- According to one tradition, Ælfwald II reigned as king of Northumbria after Eardwulf was deposed in 806.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
